    "title": "Apply referential integrity to placements",
    "commandWord": "Explain",
    "objectiveIds": [],
    "syllabusMapping": [
      "S8.02"
    ],
    "reading": [
      "Explain the consistency rule, then use a specific pair of tables from WORKEXPERIENCE."
    ],
    "solution": [
      "Referential integrity keeps related data consistent. Each non-null foreign-key value must match a referenced key. For example, PLACEMENT.CompanyID refers to COMPANY.CompanyID, so a placement cannot refer to a company that is absent."
    ],
    "marking": [
      "Three marks overall; at most two generic and at most two specific points. The response above supplies the rule and a concrete application.",
      "The official scheme includes cascading actions. In an implemented database these depend on declared update/delete rules; a foreign key can instead restrict an operation. Do not infer that all foreign keys automatically cascade."
    ],
